(7343795, 1147314, 30049, '<td valign="top">Hey!  Very cool.  :-)  Was surprised to see this on the front page given the direction the score was heading the last day.  Thanks everybody.  I smiled when I saw this photo opportunity.  Had to work around all of the jet skis out there.  Now if I could have gotten one of those going "airborne" at the same time that would have been super cool (maybe).  ;-P</td>', 'Hey!  Very cool.  :-)  Was surprised to see this on the front page given the direction the score was heading the last day.  Thanks everybody.  I smiled when I saw this photo opportunity.  Had to work around all of the jet skis out there.  Now if I could have gotten one of those going "airborne" at the same time that would have been super cool (maybe).  ;-P', '2015-04-20 08:22:25.000000', NULL, 0),
(7343796, 1147342, 180170, '<td valign="top">Shame this one didn''t do better, I liked it and I could feel the air!</td>', 'Shame this one didn''t do better, I liked it and I could feel the air!', '2015-04-20 08:29:11.000000', NULL, 0),
(7343798, 1147366, 113900, '<td valign="top">This is my favorite shot you''ve ever taken.  Not sure why the low score, DNMC maybe?  Either way it is a gorgeous photograph that deserves to be recognized as such.</td>', 'This is my favorite shot you''ve ever taken.  Not sure why the low score, DNMC maybe?  Either way it is a gorgeous photograph that deserves to be recognized as such.', '2015-04-20 08:54:19.000000', NULL, 0),
(7343799, 1147210, 69324, '<td valign="top">Beautiful</td>', 'Beautiful', '2015-04-20 08:54:24.000000', NULL, 0),
(7343804, 1147351, 69008, '<td valign="top">This one probably got dinged pretty bad as a DNMC kind of image because you were shooting downward . <br/>If you can''t get the camera low enough to get the sky, you can use a mirror to get the "shot from the viewpoint of an ant on the ground" look with the sky behind the subject. <br/>The two plant stems going across the frame at the flower also made it sort of busy looking. <br/>The 28mm macro might allow you to get in a lot closer for true "macro" shooting. <br/>Meanwhile, keep shooting. It''s interesting to watch your posts as you experiment with learning the different facets of photography. <br/>What you lack in technical skill, you more than make up for with your enthusiasm.  :  )</td>', 'This one probably got dinged pretty bad as a DNMC kind of image because you were shooting downward . If you can''t get the camera low enough to get the sky, you can use a mirror to get the "shot from the viewpoint of an ant on the ground" look with the sky behind the subject. The two plant stems going across the frame at the flower also made it sort of busy looking. The 28mm macro might allow you to get in a lot closer for true "macro" shooting. Meanwhile, keep shooting. It''s interesting to watch your posts as you experiment with learning the different facets of photography. What you lack in technical skill, you more than make up for with your enthusiasm.  :  )', '2015-04-20 09:31:20.000000', NULL, 0),
(7343805, 1147329, 69008, '<td valign="top">Well done. I understand how technically difficult and time consuming it is to do this sort of photography.</td>', 'Well done. I understand how technically difficult and time consuming it is to do this sort of photography.', '2015-04-20 09:39:27.000000', NULL, 0),
(7343807, 1147376, 69008, '<td valign="top">That''s rare air.  I like the lens choice, and the way you framed this with the rocky foreground.  <br/>I have only seen this phenomena twice in the last six years or so, and three times if you include one at night around a full moon.  <br/></td>', 'That''s rare air.  I like the lens choice, and the way you framed this with the rocky foreground.  I have only seen this phenomena twice in the last six years or so, and three times if you include one at night around a full moon.  ', '2015-04-20 09:46:47.000000', NULL, 0),
(7343809, 1147210, 12611, '<td valign="top">Definitely wondrous. Congrats on the Blue!</td>', 'Definitely wondrous. Congrats on the Blue!', '2015-04-20 10:00:34.000000', NULL, 0),
