(7343856, 1147313, 47974, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Ja-9:</b></div><hr/><i> Darn Ronnie...I was just passing through your area day before yesterday...We did drive out on the Creole Trail (Western Louisiana) and saw a few Rosettes but to far out to catch the shot...trying to see some nature vs rear ends of vehicles!!!  Great capture. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/><img alt="'' . substr(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21_F.gif'', strrpos(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21_F.gif'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21_F.gif"/> <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/profile.php?USER_ID=98339" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">Ja-9</a> There are a number of rookeries around this area and LA that have Spoonbills that are pretty easy to photograph.  Do they nest in Florida?  If so, I am sure you can find some at a rookery.  I have been chasing photos of these for awhile now and this spring finally got some photos of them.  They are so pretty and super colorful right now in their breeding plumage, as most birds are right now.<br/> <br/>Oh, if you are ever in the area again and want to get together or want to find some cool wildlife let me know.  Have a great year around spot for gators if you like them :-)<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2015-04-20 11:15:07.</i></td>', 'Originally posted by Ja-9: Darn Ronnie...I was just passing through your area day before yesterday...We did drive out on the Creole Trail (Western Louisiana) and saw a few Rosettes but to far out to catch the shot...trying to see some nature vs rear ends of vehicles!!!  Great capture.    Ja-9 There are a number of rookeries around this area and LA that have Spoonbills that are pretty easy to photograph.  Do they nest in Florida?  If so, I am sure you can find some at a rookery.  I have been chasing photos of these for awhile now and this spring finally got some photos of them.  They are so pretty and super colorful right now in their breeding plumage, as most birds are right now. Oh, if you are ever in the area again and want to get together or want to find some cool wildlife let me know.  Have a great year around spot for gators if you like them :-)', '2015-04-20 11:57:14.000000', '2015-04-20 12:15:07.000000', 0),
